==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|rihtec}}, from {{inh|de|goh|rihtīg}}, from {{m|goh|reht||right}} + {{m|goh|-ig}}. Equivalent to {{suf|de|recht|ig}}. Originally only an adjective; adverb developed later.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʁɪçtɪç/|a=standard}}
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʁɪçtɪk/|a=southern Germany,Austria,Switzerland}}
* {{audio|de|De-richtig.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-richtig2.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-richtig3.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-richtig.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{hyphenation|de|rich|tig}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɪçtɪç}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|comp}}

# [[correct]], [[accurate]], [[right]]
#: {{ux|de|eine richtige Antwort|a correct answer}}
# [[right]], [[correct]], [[good]]
#: {{ux|de|die richtige Entscheidung|the right choice}}
# [[right]], [[fit]], [[appropriate]]
#: {{ux|de|der richtige Mann für den Job|the right man for the job}}
# [[proper]], [[real]], [[actual]]
#: {{ux|de|ihr richtiger Name|her actual name}}
# [[proper]], [[real]], [[respectable]], [[reputable]]
#: {{ux|de|ein richtiger Job, ein richtiger Mann|a proper job, a real man}}
# [[complete]], [[real]], [[downright]], [[just]]
#: {{ux|de|ein richtiges Arschloch|a complete asshole}}

====Declension====
{{de-adecl|comp}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[really]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich habe manchmal ein '''richtig''' schlechtes Gefühl.|Sometimes I have a really bad feeling.}}

